# Live system
live-boot
live-boot-initramfs-tools
live-config
live-config-systemd
zstd

# Networking: NetworkManager for ethernet/wifi, tor for everything outbound,
# nftables to make "everything outbound = tor" structural rather than advisory.
network-manager
tor
obfs4proxy
nftables
curl
ca-certificates

# NVIDIA proprietary - DKMS builds against the live kernel at image-build time.
# Secure Boot must be OFF on the target machine (the module is unsigned).
# Ships 550.163.01 (verified inside a built ISO, Aug 2026): Maxwell (GTX 900)
# through Ada (RTX 40).
#
# RTX 50-series / Blackwell needs driver 570+, and Debian packages NOTHING newer
# than 550 anywhere - trixie, trixie-backports, sid and forky all resolve to
# 550.163.01 (all four checked). So there is no apt-based fix: a 50-series card
# falls back to CPU until Debian ships 570+. Do not "just add backports" - it is
# the same driver.
#
# Intel/older GPUs: CPU inference. AMD is handled via ROCm below, not here.
nvidia-driver
linux-headers-amd64
firmware-misc-nonfree
firmware-linux
# AMD: amdgpu is in-kernel, but the compute stack needs the firmware blobs.
# Pairs with the ROCm tarball in the payload (ROCM=0 at build time drops both).
firmware-amd-graphics
intel-microcode
amd64-microcode

# The tool
python3
python3-requests
python3-socks

# Console
sudo
nano
micro
gpm
less
procps
pciutils
kbd

# Printing - driverless-first (IPP Everywhere/AirPrint over network or USB),
# foomatic PPDs for older kit. The firewall keeps all of this sealed behind
# the onionmind.print boot flag except USB, which needs no network at all.
cups
cups-client
cups-filters
cups-browsed
ipp-usb
foomatic-db-engine
foomatic-db
